package CanvasNet {
    part def LegendBuilder {
        doc /* The internal LegendPlan, LegendBuilder, and their records, own C# implementations with attribution of the legend rules of Vega-Lite and Vega: LegendPlan decides which of the channels color, size, shape, fill, stroke, strokeDash, strokeWidth, and opacity have a legend (a field or datum with a scale, unless the legend or scale is null or config.legend.disable is set), the kind of each (a gradient for a continuous color scale, a discrete gradient for a quantize, quantile, or threshold color scale, symbols otherwise), its orient and direction, its title, and merges channels whose domains are the same (the first channel is the canonical scale); LegendBuilder builds one legend as a legend group with a legend-entry group and a legend-title text - symbol legends with an entry per value (a domain, d3 ticks, or the classes of a discretizing scale with range labels, limited by symbolLimit with a final entry that counts the rest), laid out by the grid layout of Vega with rows of 2 and columns of 10 pixels, and gradient legends with a bar filled by a linear gradient whose stops are the ends of the domain and the ticks for a count of 15 (Vega scaleGradient), tick labels outside the bar thinned by LabelOverlap, or one band per class - and measures the box it needs from the entries, the title, and the padding. The unit fails with a located VegaLiteRenderException naming the limit when the values, ticks, label text, or scene items exceed MaxScaleDomainSize, MaxTicks, MaxStringLength, or MaxSceneItems (every scene item is charged before it is created, every loop polls the cancellation token), and with a located VegaLiteSpecException for an invalid format. The gradient stops and labels of a log, pow, sqrt, or symlog scale are placed along the transformed domain, and a log legend labels only the log ticks that Vega labels. The symbol legend of a bin-ordinal scale (a binned color) has one entry per bin labeled with the range of the bin, and the channels of the same binned field share one legend. A condition that holds a field has a legend of its field, conditions that hold only values have none, and the symbols of another legend show the first condition value and the largest opacity. Text is measured with the bundled fonts only. */

        comment sourceRef /* Source: src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/Guides/LegendPlan.cs, LegendBuilder.cs, LegendBuilder.Symbols.cs, LegendBuilder.Gradient.cs, and LegendBuilder.Grid.cs */
        comment testRef /* Test: test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/Guides/LegendPlanTests.cs, LegendBuilderTests.cs, and LegendPlanConditionTests.cs */
        comment designRef /* Design: docs/design/canvas-net-vega-lite/guides/legend-builder.md */
        comment verificationRef /* Verification: docs/verification/canvas-net-vega-lite/guides/legend-builder.md */
        comment reqRef /* Requirements: docs/reqstream/canvas-net-vega-lite/guides/legend-builder.yaml */
    }
}
